an5.78:4.3 | S: But there will come a time of peril due to turmoil in the wilds, so the countryfolk mount their vehicles and flee everywhere. | T: The time will come, though, when there is danger & an invasion of savage tribes. Taking power, they will surround the countryside.
an5.78:4.4 | S: In a time of peril, people move to where there’s sanctuary, | T: When there is danger, people will congregate where it is safe.
an5.78:4.5 | S: where they live crowded and cramped together. | T: There they will live packed & crowded together.
an5.78:4.6 | S: When you live crowded and cramped together, it’s not easy to focus on the instructions of the Buddhas, and it’s not easy to frequent remote lodgings in the wilderness and the forest. | T: When one is living packed & crowded together, it is not easy to pay attention to the Buddha’s teachings. It is not easy to reside in isolated forest or wilderness dwellings.
an5.78:4.7 | S: Before that unlikable, undesirable, and disagreeable thing happens, | T: Before this unwelcome, disagreeable, displeasing thing happens,
